@startuml gas-phase-vacancy
' SPEC: _spec/packages/starchess-core/gas-phase-vacancy.puml
' purpose: phase-aware vacancy (binding refinement) — only Marine stimStep + BattleShip tacticalJump vacate; transit vs origin matrix + canonical chains.
' covers: packages/starchess-core/src/resolve/submit-turn.ts
' covers: packages/starchess-core/src/resolve/resolve-turn.ts
' covers: packages/starchess-core/src/rules/validation.ts
' covers: packages/starchess-core/src/board/moves.ts
' covers: apps/starchess/src/presentation/specials/planning/occupancy.ts
' covers: apps/starchess/src/presentation/combat/intentOverlays.ts
' see also: _spec/packages/starchess-core/resolve.puml
' see also: _spec/packages/starchess-core/resolve-turn-activity.puml
' see also: _spec/packages/starchess-core/sc-moves.puml
' see also: _spec/apps/starchess/core/board/planning-projection.puml
' see also: _spec/packages/starchess-core/turn-queue-sequence.puml
' see also: _spec/packages/starchess-core/mine-contact.puml
!include ../../themes/proveo.puml

skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam defaultTextAlignment left

title StarChess Core · Gas-phase vacancy (required)

package "packages/starchess-core — order + rules" {
  component "resolve/submit-turn.ts\nendScTurn — order owner" as SUB <<app>>
  component "resolve/resolve-turn.ts\nRULES + relocate" as RES <<app>>
  component "rules/validation.ts\nassertClassicalBaseline" as VAL <<error>>
  component "board/moves.ts\nscMovesFrom" as MOV <<app>>
  database "placement map\nstart board" as MAP <<db>>
}

package "apps/starchess — planning chrome" {
  component "presentation/specials/planning\noccupancyForQueuedMoves" as OCC <<app>>
  component "presentation/combat\nintentOverlaysFromQueue" as OV <<app>>
}

SUB ARROW_MAIN RES : B < C < F rank order
SUB ARROW_MAIN VAL : queue + placement
VAL ARROW_ERROR RES : ally aim rejected today
VAL ARROW_OPTIONAL MAP : reads live placement
RES ARROW_MAIN MAP : ordered relocate
MOV ARROW_OPTIONAL OCC : reads projected map
OCC ARROW_MAIN OV : ghosts paint vacancy
OV ARROW_OPTIONAL RES : never resolves

note as N_ORDER
  Turn order remains exclusively
  owned by ""endScTurn"" sequencing.
  Preliminary checks open, B combat
  precedes C, and F concludes last.
end note
N_ORDER .. SUB

note as N_VACATE
  Only Marine stimStep advance
  relinquishes origin with gas, as
  does BattleShip tacticalJump transit.
  Spawn crushes arrival instead, and
  mine, siege, snipe never vacate.
end note
N_VACATE .. RES

note as N_CURRENT
  B departure origin becomes FREE
  for both C and F later landings.
  Validation consults projection, not
  live placement, for ally occupancy.
end note
N_CURRENT .. VAL

note as N_TRANSIT
  B arrival plus rewritten C origin
  counts as transit, never vacancy.
  C landing there stays BLOCKED, as
  transit evaluation precedes origin
  departure permission instead.
end note
N_TRANSIT .. VAL

note as N_MOVE_GAS
  Rewritten C departure frees origin
  for later F arrival in mirror.
  F departure itself stays terminal,
  chaining only toward later F in one
  sequence, never toward prior phases.
end note
N_MOVE_GAS .. RES

note as N_ORDERING
  B chain applies heads first under
  departure ordering, never overwrite.
  Consequently e2 to e3 plus e3 to e4
  both commit same phase, each arrival
  pursuing its vacater sequentially.
end note
N_ORDERING .. SUB

note as N_WARP
  BattleShip warp departure frees its
  origin for later phases likewise.
  Warp arrival onto holdout remains
  rejected, since movement never
  crushes through resident pieces.
end note
N_WARP .. RES

note as N_CANON_AB
  Canonical B e2 to e3 plus rewritten
  C e3 to e4 onward chains advance.
  Command Center e1 to e2 lands validated
  vacant, while e1 to e3 disqualifies
  since transit precludes entry sequentially.
end note
N_CANON_AB .. RES

note as N_CANON_CD
  Move plus gas mirrors advance with
  C e2 to e3 then F e3 to e4 onward.
  Warp origin frees symmetrically, yet
  warp arrival onto holdout remains
  rejected since relocation crushes no residents.
end note
N_CANON_CD .. RES

note as N_PROJ
  Planning projection paints post-B
  vacancy as selectable destination.
  Ghosts follow folded queue order, yet
  only resolve owns collision outcomes.
end note
N_PROJ .. OV
@enduml
